1
00:00:06,418 --> 00:00:09,481
A painted rice cake
does not satisfy hunger.

2
00:00:10,297 --> 00:00:12,051
So says an old Zen warning.

3
00:00:12,131 --> 00:00:14,035
Concepts are pictures of food.

4
00:00:14,115 --> 00:00:16,005
Realisation is eating.

5
00:00:16,085 --> 00:00:19,021
The monk Xiangyan,
famous for his learning,

6
00:00:19,101 --> 00:00:22,839
could not answer his teacher's
question, and burned his notes.

7
00:00:22,919 --> 00:00:28,919
Years later, sweeping a path, he heard a
pebble strike a stalk of bamboo. He woke.

8
00:00:29,789 --> 00:00:32,046
Dōgen turns the saying over.

9
00:00:32,126 --> 00:00:37,793
In Gabyō, a chapter of his Shōbōgenzō, he
writes that there is no remedy for hunger

10
00:00:37,873 --> 00:00:40,008
other than painted rice cakes.

11
00:00:40,088 --> 00:00:44,876
Without painted hunger, he says,
one never becomes a true person.

12
00:00:45,694 --> 00:00:48,332
He is not praising study over practice.

13
00:00:48,412 --> 00:00:51,217
He is refusing the
picture behind the saying:

14
00:00:51,346 --> 00:00:55,560
a real, unpainted cake
on one side, and pale,

15
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,833
useless paintings of it on the other.

16
00:00:58,645 --> 00:01:00,426
Look for the unpainted one.

17
00:01:00,506 --> 00:01:02,722
Take the next thing you are about to eat,

18
00:01:02,802 --> 00:01:05,032
a rice cake or a piece of bread.

19
00:01:05,112 --> 00:01:07,980
It appears, first of all, as food.

20
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:12,654
Not as a white, roughly round object
that you then recognise as edible.

21
00:01:12,734 --> 00:01:16,599
It is already something to eat,
already pulling at the hand.

22
00:01:17,417 --> 00:01:22,377
Now remove that. Remove the name, and
the knowing that it is made from rice.

23
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:24,810
Remove the hunger that makes it look good.

24
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:30,149
Remove the occasions it belongs to, the
New Year table, the snack at your desk.

25
00:01:30,229 --> 00:01:34,198
Remove the farmer, the field,
the hand that pounded it.

26
00:01:34,278 --> 00:01:36,757
What is left that is the rice cake itself?

27
00:01:37,557 --> 00:01:41,607
Each place you look yields more
appearance, and no cake behind it.

28
00:01:41,687 --> 00:01:44,950
To a stone, nothing on
the plate is food at all.

29
00:01:45,030 --> 00:01:47,776
To an ant, it is a mountain of sugar.

30
00:01:47,856 --> 00:01:51,720
A rice cake apart from every
way of meeting it is not found.

31
00:01:52,537 --> 00:01:56,302
Dōgen is not saying there is
nothing but the mind's painting.

32
00:01:56,382 --> 00:01:59,019
There is no blank canvas
under the painting,

33
00:01:59,099 --> 00:02:01,492
and no painter standing apart from it.

34
00:02:01,572 --> 00:02:05,840
In this book's reading, the painting
is how anything is met at all.

35
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,688
And the painted cake feeds.

36
00:02:07,768 --> 00:02:09,780
Eat it, and the hunger goes.

37
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:14,468
What is removed is only the assumption
that an unpainted cake must be doing the

38
00:02:14,548 --> 00:02:15,994
feeding underneath.

39
00:02:16,805 --> 00:02:19,293
Then Dōgen goes one step further.

40
00:02:19,373 --> 00:02:21,032
The hunger is painted too.

41
00:02:21,112 --> 00:02:24,007
Hunger is named together with
the food that would end it,

42
00:02:24,087 --> 00:02:29,456
just as fuel is fuel only as what
fire burns. Neither comes first.

43
00:02:29,536 --> 00:02:31,534
Yet hunger is no less real.

44
00:02:31,614 --> 00:02:33,332
It gets you up from the desk.

45
00:02:34,137 --> 00:02:37,182
Xiangyan was not wrong to burn his notes.

46
00:02:37,262 --> 00:02:41,353
He burned the use he had made of
them, as a substitute for seeing.

47
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:43,160
The cure was not a better note.

48
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:45,039
It was the pebble on the bamboo.

49
00:02:45,866 --> 00:02:49,197
But awakening does not
lie beyond all painting,

50
00:02:49,277 --> 00:02:51,330
in some unpainted ground.

51
00:02:51,410 --> 00:02:55,284
The sound of the pebble was
painted too: heard as a click,

52
00:02:55,364 --> 00:02:57,471
as the end of a long search.

53
00:02:57,551 --> 00:03:00,039
Realisation did not escape the painting.

54
00:03:00,119 --> 00:03:02,815
It saw through the demand
for something behind it.

55
00:03:03,617 --> 00:03:05,262
Try this over one meal.

56
00:03:05,342 --> 00:03:08,265
Before eating, notice
how the food appears:

57
00:03:08,345 --> 00:03:10,982
already as food, already wanted.

58
00:03:11,062 --> 00:03:14,732
Then look, slowly, for the
food apart from its name,

59
00:03:14,812 --> 00:03:16,920
its history and its use.

60
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,781
Look at the hunger the same way.

61
00:03:18,861 --> 00:03:22,762
Where is it, apart from the
food, the stomach, the hour?

62
00:03:22,842 --> 00:03:25,104
Then put the looking down, and eat.

63
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:29,016
The meal is exactly as
satisfying as before.

64
00:03:29,096 --> 00:03:34,279
Painted food, painted hunger, painted
satisfaction, and nothing missing.

